# Design

Vision Studio fills the viewport. The ground is `#0A0A12`, with film grain at 2% opacity and a soft violet radial glow behind the main area. Cards are `#12121C`, with a 1px border `rgba(167,139,250,0.12)` and an inner gradient from `rgba(139,92,246,0.06)` to transparent. Raised controls are `#1A1A27`. Hover surfaces are `#20202F`. Primary text is `#EEEDF7`. Secondary text is `#A6A3BF`. Readable muted text is `#7E7A9C`. On violet `#8B5CF6`, text is `#0A0A12`. On `#2E1F5E`, text is `#EEEDF7`. Text pairs are at least 4.5 to 1. `#6F6C8A` fails that on a card, at about 3.8 to 1, so it is for non-text marks only.

Violet `#8B5CF6` is the accent and the filled primary action. `#A78BFA` is for gradients, the readout glow, focus, and the thinking light. `#2E1F5E` is a filled background. Cyan `#5EEAD4` is only for detected values and success, including the ready light. Status lights: idle uses the quiet mark, thinking `#A78BFA` pulsing, ready `#5EEAD4`, error `#F87171`. A thin diagonal stripe may run on the top edge of a card while thinking or rendering. Readout numbers may glow faintly. Nothing else glows.

Lane colours appear only on audio, waveforms, and a selected layer pill: drums `#F07167`, chords `#F2C14E`, bass `#4FD1A5`, melody `#7AA2FF`, texture `#C084FC`. A waveform runs from `#8B5CF6` into the lane colour. Full mix uses light violet, not a sixth hue.

General Sans is the interface. Martian Mono is readout values, file names, and the trace. Both are self hosted. Sentence case. No all caps. Tabular numbers. Eyebrow 12px medium in light violet, page title 30px semibold, card titles 15px semibold, body 14px with line height 1.55, small text 12px, readout values 26px. Icons are lucide, 16px, with an 8px gap to the label. Every icon button has a label or a tooltip.

Spacing is 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, and 32. Cards are 16px radius with 20px padding. Readout tiles are 112px tall, with 12px vertical padding and 20px horizontal padding. Controls are 10px radius. Pills are fully round. Hover is 150ms. Focus is a 1px `#A78BFA` ring. Reduced motion stops the stripe, the tip rotation, and holds the thinking light and dots steady.

The sidebar is 248px and flush left on Create and Genres: a waveform mark beside Vision Studio, then Home, Create, Genres, and Analyse and Tweak with a Soon pill, recent ideas, a tip, and Help. It collapses to icons under 1024px, with tooltips. Labels stay at 1280px. Home is the landing at /, without the sidebar. Create keeps the header and a centred column of at most 760px. Tempo, key, bars, and coverage are one slim row. A value appears only when it is known. Brief, layers, and the trace open from a Brief button. When the brief is ready, the column gives way to a full-width review. After Build, the main area is the results list and the player. The thread and the results list are the inner scrollers. Home and Create fade and lift 12px over 220ms. Reduced motion stays still.

Create uses the same header: eyebrow, title, subtitle, actions on the right. Home's primary action is Start training. A secondary Create button sits with it, and the composer still submits into Create. The create header has a Brief button, the session status, and one filled Build now button. The only exact "Build" is the primary button on the review footer, once prompts exist. Write prompts is that primary button until then. The brief does not repeat tempo, key, or bars. Empty groups are hidden. Before any input it says "Details appear here as we talk." The empty thread states the contract and holds the example chips. The first reply reflects the producer's words, states a draft, and asks at most one question. It does not ask which layers to make.

The question bubble is the only polite live region. Send's accessible name is "Send the idea". The All layers pill does not read "all layers separately". `data-variant` stays on every take. The composer stays mounted. Colours, spacing, radius, and type live as CSS variables, and Tailwind reads the same theme.
